  "notes": [
    "Each measured case runs the shipped solver and an independent recomputation inside the page. Inputs, measured value, reference value and tolerance are recorded per check, so any measured verdict can be reproduced by calling window.__dgcBenchmark() on the tool.",
    "Recorded cases carry reference_provenance \"recorded\". They rest on official IAPWS program-verification points, an external HEM experimental dataset, an isolated-VM Worker run and a canonical DiagramCompute runtime, none of which this page can evaluate. Their inputs and comparison rows are null because no measurement was made here.",
    "The Lin-Gruen-Quapp HEM envelope case remains a failing model-envelope warning. No empirical correction has been fitted to it.",
    "Revision 2026-09-11 corrects the two numerical defects this artifact recorded as failures on 2026-09-05. discharge() solves the pipe resistance relation on the bracket [0, mdot_nozzle] rather than by a damped fixed point capped at ten iterations. solve() puts the saturated-vapour crossing of the equilibrium two-phase inventory on a step boundary, with the locateEvent() call the single-phase inventory model already used for the same crossing; the mass flow steps by a measured 4.81 % there, because steamNozzle() hands a two-phase upstream state to the equilibrium HEM nozzle instead of the metastable isentrope. energyPartials() takes its finite differences on one side of that surface, where dU/dT is 3.621e3 J/K on the superheated side and 1.372e5 J/K on the two-phase side. The embedded Python export carries the same three changes; browser/Python agreement over four scenarios is 7.75e-10 relative.",
    "The equilibrium two-phase terminal time settles near 1e-3 s under further partition refinement rather than at zero. Two non-smoothnesses remain in that branch and neither shrinks with the step: the nozzle isentrope crosses from stable IF97 Region 2 into the metastable-vapour supplement with a 1.56e-4 relative step in mass flow, and steamHemCritical() maximises the HEM mass flux on a 96-point log-pressure grid, which moves the located critical state by up to 3.0e-6 relative between neighbouring states."
  ]
